From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: s5l8960x-j72: Add Lightning charging

iBoot leaves the D2089's input-current limit at 100 mA (0x4c0 = 0x02),
so the iPad Air drains on a cable. Describe the Tristar (CBTL1610) at
i2c2 0x1a, the D2089's PMU event controller on AP GPIO 103 (the ADT pmu
node's interrupt) and the Lightning charger on the PMIC with the PMU
line (112) and ADC done (89). Link the charger to the USB device
controller, which reports the host's allowance to it and whose data
role the charger sets.

The ADT's charger node allows 0x960 = 2400 mA of input. The board
maximum is 1050 mA instead, the highest limit measured on a J72: code
0x4e charged the battery at +279 to +423 mA under the desktop, at
35.8-36.1 C, in thisiscamk's ten-minute run on a powered hub port, and
the limit went back to 0x02 on unplug. A higher maximum waits for a
measurement.

No source events, as on the iPad Air 2: the charger's 100 ms poll of the
connection state sees plug and unplug.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-j72.dts | 62 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 62 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-j72.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-j72.dts
index cd88b7643..c3e77d855 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-j72.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-j72.dts
@@ -74,6 +74,68 @@
 		compatible = "apple,d2089-touch-core-regulator";
 		regulator-name = "touch-core";
 	};
+
+	/* The PMU event line, from the ADT pmu node: AP GPIO 103. */
+	pmu_events: interrupt-controller {
+		compatible = "apple,d2089-pmic-gpio";
+		interrupt-controller;
+		#interrupt-cells = <2>;
+		interrupts-extended = <&pinctrl 103 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+	};
+
+	/*
+	 * Lightning charging, at the D2089's registers as iOS 12.5.7
+	 * AppleD2089PMUPowerSource uses them: connection and charger state
+	 * at 0x60, the input-current limit at 0x4c0, the ADC at 0x500.
+	 *
+	 * The ADT's charger node allows 0x960 = 2400 mA of input. The board
+	 * maximum here is the highest input limit measured on a J72 so far:
+	 * 1050 mA (0x4e) charged the battery at +279 to +423 mA under the
+	 * desktop, at 36 C, in thisiscamk's ten-minute run.
+	 */
+	tristar_charger: charger@60 {
+		compatible = "apple,j72-tristar-charger", "apple,d2089-tristar-charger";
+		reg = <0x60 0x0d>, <0x4c0 0x01>, <0x500 0x04>;
+		reg-names = "status", "control", "adc";
+		interrupt-parent = <&pmu_events>;
+		/*
+		 * The PMU line and ADC done. No source events, as on the iPad
+		 * Air 2: the charger's 100 ms poll of 0x60 sees plug and unplug.
+		 */
+		interrupts = <112 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+			     <89 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+		apple,tristar = <&tristar>;
+		input-current-limit-microamp = <1050000>;
+
+		/* The charger decides when USB data may come on. */
+		port {
+			tristar_charger_usb: endpoint {
+				remote-endpoint = <&usbdev_role>;
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&i2c2 {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	/* The Lightning port controller, from the ADT i2c2/tristar node. */
+	tristar: port-controller@1a {
+		compatible = "nxp,cbtl1610";
+		reg = <0x1a>;
+	};
+};
+
+/* Tell the Lightning charger what the USB host allows. */
+&usbdev {
+	usb-psy-name = "lightning";
+	usb-role-switch;
+
+	port {
+		usbdev_role: endpoint {
+			remote-endpoint = <&tristar_charger_usb>;
+		};
+	};
 };
 
 &ps_ans {
